Soundtrack import: <game> --import-soundtrack <folder> builds the game's music
from the player's own copy of its soundtrack (any format FFmpeg reads): finds
each album track, lines it up with the game's track (FFT cross-correlation, or a
recipe of sections for tracks the game edited), matches its level and writes
<key>.flac into soundtrack/ in the game folder or the per-user data folder,
with soundtrack.txt as the report. The game plays those files when
audio.soundtrack is on (<prefix>_SOUNDTRACK; default on), FLAC or WAVE;
<prefix>_MUSIC_DIR still overrides the folder. GameProfile gains
soundtrack_music (the game's tracks from its disc image) and soundtrack_table
(names, lengths and offsets only; no audio). Windows: links avformat, avfilter
and swresample from the same LGPL FFmpeg prebuilt and ships avformat-61,
avfilter-10 and swscale-8. Entries with game_frames/game_rms are built from
the album alone (VC3, whose music the import can't read). Needs 0040. (2026-11-25)

